                ],
                "fontFamily": "Inter",
                "text": "The first-run state, and the reason the ordinal changes tone: an unnamed chip carries `input 3` in the PRIMARY ink because it is the only thing the chip says, while a named one drops it to grey under the name. Held at grey throughout, a rig where nothing is named would be a grid of entirely grey chips \u2014 which reads as disabled rather than as nothing having been said about them yet. The row above reads `none named` (#528)."
              }
            ],
